#: ../../source/path-exists_readme.md:3
msgid "Check if a path exists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-exists_readme.md:5
msgid ""
"Because "
"[`fs.exists()`](https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#fs_fs_exists_path_callback)"
" is being [deprecated](https://github.com/iojs/io.js/issues/103), but "
"there's still a genuine use-case of being able to check if a path exists "
"for other purposes than doing IO with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-exists_readme.md:7
msgid "Never use this before handling a file though:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/path-exists_readme.md:9
msgid ""
"In particular, checking if a file exists before opening it is an anti-"
"pattern that leaves you vulnerable to race conditions: another process "
"may remove the file between the calls to `fs.exists()` and `fs.open()`. "
"Just open the file and handle the error when it's not there."
msgstr ""

